#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD9723 expect=skipped domain=SE
#note "The discriminator that keeps the family from double-reporting: the SEUPDES column EXISTS (blank on the unplanned row), so Requirements.Variables.None [SEUPDES] skips this sister with a reason naming the column, and the parents PMDA-SD0092 and PMDA-SD1266 own the case, reporting row 2 with its location."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col SEUPDES type=Char label="Description of Unplanned Element"
---
S1 | SE | 001 | 1 | SCRN   | Screening         |
S1 | SE | 001 | 2 | UNPLAN | Unplanned Element |
